  "localContent": "Extreme close crop of existing south CITY WALL, NOT plaza floor or whole building. Same native-scale pale natural grey/beige limestone, rounded hand-painted bevels, restrained mineral variation matching actual anchors. No gritty noise, no photoreal plastic, no standalone props/trees/pots/buildings/text/UI. Native anchors override coarse guide joint positions: true mortar continues across x115/y115 and x230/y230 until actual stone-course boundaries. Anchor edge is never an object edge, no short isolated joint, no straight texture/value stripe. Lower pale wall with inherited full-width courses around y245/y548, pale footing y1015..1148, dark grey foundation only bottom. Faint green grey weathering lower center okay; no whole plant.\nMANDATORY: This crop is a flat wall far BELOW the parapet, with no top edge visible. NO RAILING, no balusters, no wall cap, no sky, no visible wall top. Keep top native 230 pixels exactly as supplied, which is flat stone all the way to the image top. The entire crop contains only these wall courses: y0..245 flat unbroken limestone with NO vertical joint, y245..548 limestone course, y548..1015 one continuous large limestone course. The ONLY horizontal mortar levels are y245 and548; a projecting footing begins y1015 and ends1148, then dark foundation. No joint at y840, no orphan lines ending at x230. x230 and y230 are invisible crop edges, never objects. Sparse staggered vertical mortar may occur only inside courses and connect their true horizontal boundaries. Entire surface is close-up warm hand-painted stone wall, never complete architectural object. Preserve native left/top geometry; coarse blur is placement only.",
